= Training set =

== Overview ==
A '''training set''' is the data used directly to fit a model's parameters, representations, rules, or policy.

Training data influence the learned system through the learning procedure itself.

== Fitting ==
Depending on the method, training can involve:

* gradient updates;
* likelihood or loss minimization;
* rule induction;
* tree splitting;
* prototype construction;
* representation learning;
* policy optimization.

The defining feature is direct influence on the fitted model.

== Data roles ==
A dataset can be partitioned into [[Training set|training]], [[Validation set|validation]], and [[Test set|test]] roles.

These roles are defined by use, not by fixed percentages.

Cross-validation can rotate observations through training and validation roles.

== Preprocessing ==
Preprocessing steps that estimate statistics from data—such as normalization, feature selection, imputation, or dimensionality reduction—must be treated as part of the fitting pipeline.

Estimating them using held-out test data can cause [[Data leakage (machine learning)|data leakage]].

== Related concepts ==
[[Machine learning]], [[Validation set]], [[Test set]], [[Overfitting]], [[Provenance]], and [[Data leakage (machine learning)]] define the surrounding evaluation pipeline.

